R"VG(
# watermark_far.vg (Z-06): a made species' watermark (watermark.vg's root): what it was made for, by how it lives (`madeway`), where
# (`madeplace`) and whether its crowd glows (`madeglow`), in either age; and the far future's own (`wm.ff.`: no names but where they are
# owed, the life left to itself). Every word apart, every long sentence of parts.
@apart

# ---- what it was made for -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wm.for
  (madeway=light) {wm.open} {wm.light.work}{wm.why}.
  (madeway=chemical) {wm.open} {wm.chem.work}{wm.why}.
  (madeway=dead) {wm.open} {wm.dead.work}{wm.why}.
  (madeway=grazer|madeway=predator) {wm.open} {wm.eat.work}{wm.why}.
  (2 madeglow=1) {wm.open} light {wm.glowplace} without fire{wm.why}.
  (1.5 stage>=1) {wm.late}
wm.open
  It was made to
  We made it to
  Its work is to
  It was grown to
  It was written to
  We wrote it to
  The first of it was let loose to
  (age=farfuture) It was made, long ago, to
  (age=farfuture) Once, it was meant to
wm.why
  , because nothing else would grow there
  , after the {wm.harm}
  , while there was still time
  , as {$home} had asked
  , because the machines had failed at it
  , when the {wm.harm} would not end
  , for the children of {wm.place}
  ; it did, for longer than we hoped
  ; for a while it did
  ; it is doing it still, if you can read this
  ; we never knew whether it would
  , and it asks only for {wm.food}
  , in the dark, for as long as there is anything there to eat
  (1)
wm.light.work
  make air again over {wm.ruined}
  green {wm.ruined}
  feed the ponds of {wm.place}
  cover {wm.ruined} before the soil could blow away
  turn the light into food in the {fut.green} of {wm.place}
  give {wm.place} back the colour it had
  thicken {wm.waters} until {fish} could live there again
  hold the sand of {wm.ruined} together
  feed the {herd} when the grass failed
  grow under {crop} and keep the ground wet
wm.chem.work
  eat the metals the old works left in {wm.waters}
  take the poison out of {wm.waters}
  keep {wm.waters} sweet
  gather [copper|iron|silver|the rare metals] out of {wm.waters} into its own walls
  close the old mines under {mountain} from the inside
  clean the deep water under {wm.place}
  turn the gas of the old wells into something that does not burn
  feed on the stone of {wm.ruined} and leave soil behind
wm.dead.work
  turn the waste of {wm.place} back into soil
  break down {wm.waste}
  eat {wm.waste} until nothing of it was left
  clear {wm.waters} of {wm.waste}
  feed the {fut.green} with {wm.waste}
  rot the old fields of {crop} into new ones
  eat the dead {herd} before the sickness could spread
wm.eat.work
  hunt the sickness in {wm.waters}
  keep the blooms in {wm.waters} down
  eat the slime that choked {wm.waters}
  clear the rot out of the fields of {crop}
  eat the small things that sickened the {herd}
  graze the fouled ponds of {wm.place} clean
  keep the {pest} out of the stores of {crop}
wm.glowplace
  the streets of {wm.place}
  the [halls|stairs|tunnels] under {wm.place}
  the water gardens of {city2}
  the long nights at {wm.place}
  the {fut.green} in winter
wm.late
  (cause=climate|cause=drying) It was made to hold the soil when the rains {wm.rains}{wm.why}.
  (cause=poisoned|cause=nuclear|cause=weapons) It was made to eat the poison that the end left in {wm.waters}{wm.why}.
  We made it to outlast us{wm.why}.
  When we are gone something of ours should still be alive {wm.still}, and this is it.
  We made it because there was nothing else left {wm.left}.
wm.rains
  failed
  stopped coming
  came all at once
wm.still
  here
  by {water}
  in the {fut.green}
  under {mountain}
wm.left
  that we could make
  for us to do
  that would last
wm.ruined
  the dry lands round {wm.place}
  the old mines under {mountain}
  the scorched fields by {wm.waters}
  the bare slopes of {mountain}
  the grey shore of {water}
  the old fields of {crop}
  (desert=1) the salt pans
  (cold=1) the frozen marshes
wm.waters
  {water}
  the deep water under {wm.place}
  the canals of {wm.place}
  (madeplace=ice) the ice of the far north
  (madeplace=salt) the brine pools
  (madeplace=spring) the hot springs under {mountain}
  (madeplace=rock) the cracks in the rock under {wm.place}
  (madeplace=soil) the soil of {wm.place}
wm.food
  a little [salt|iron|ash|water]
  the dust of {wm.place}
  what the rain brings
wm.waste
  the plastics of the old century
  the ash of the burning years
  the tar of the old roads
  the drowned cities' rubbish
  what the factories by {wm.waters} left
  the old cloth and the old ropes
  the sludge under {wm.place}

# ---- the far future ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

wm.ff.head (formula)
  A signature, at {$home}.
  We were here. This is how you will know.
  Read slowly. This is the only part of it that was meant to be read.
  At {$home}, once. This is a signature.
  A mark, left at {$home} where a mark would last.

wm.ff.end (formula)
  The signature repeats.
  It repeats, as everything alive does.
  That is the whole of it.
  Read on, and it says this again.

wm.ff.what
  (2) {wm.ff.it} {wm.ff.is}, {wm.ff.and}.
  {wm.ff.it} {wm.ff.is}. {wm.ff.short}
wm.ff.it
  This life
  This small thing
  What carries these words
  The life you have opened
  The cell that carries this
wm.ff.is
  is ours the way a song is its singer's
  was left to chance, all but this
  could have been made in any shape, and we made it small
  was the last thing we made with our hands
  carries no law and no instruction, only this
  was small enough to last
  has no use now that we know of
  outlived the {fut.sys.n} that grew it
  was grown once at {$home} and never again
wm.ff.and
  and it no longer needs us
  and that was the intention
  and we let it be
  and nothing else of ours is as old
  and we did not mind
  and we signed it
wm.ff.short
  That is all.
  It needs nothing.
  We let it go.
  It was enough.
  (1)

wm.ff.say
  (2) {wm.ff.th} {wm.ff.short}
  {wm.ff.say.lead} {proverb}.
  We did not leave a saying. Sayings are for the living.
wm.ff.say.lead
  If you need a saying, take the old one:
  The old ones' saying was this, and we kept it:
  Our first makers would have said that
wm.ff.th
  {wm.ff.th.a}, {wm.ff.th.b}.
wm.ff.th.a
  Nothing copied for ever stays the same
  The smallest things last the longest
  What is copied is remembered
  A life is not a message, though it can carry one
  Every made thing is a question
  A signature is a kind of hope
  The wild made everything else here
  The letters outlast the hand that wrote them
  What we made small is all that is left
  A thing that copies itself is never finished
wm.ff.th.b
  and that is the beauty of it
  or so we believed
  we thought
  as our makers said
  if we were right
  and this one is ours
  in the end
  which is enough

wm.ff.reader
  {wm.ff.r.a} {wm.ff.r.b}
wm.ff.r.a
  You owe us nothing.
  Let it live.
  Read on, or do not.
  It will not mind.
  Be gentle.
  Leave it be.
wm.ff.r.b
  {wm.ff.r.if}, {wm.ff.r.then}.
  (2)
wm.ff.r.if
  If you are reading this
  Since you have read so far
  Whoever you are
  If this reached you
  If anyone reads it
  Now that you have it
wm.ff.r.then
  something of our kind is still at work in the dark
  you have read further than we expected anyone to
  we never thought of you, and yet here you are
  the life did what it was made for
  you know the last thing we wanted said
  you are the end of a long line of copies
  we were not the last to wonder

wm.ff.signed
  {$me:name} wrote these words; the rest of it wrote itself.
  {$me:name} chose the words at the last.
  {$me:name} signed it for all of us.
)VG"
